course: dictionary
lesson: 2990
title: A duke is very high in rank
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A duke is a man of very high rank. He is just below a prince, and in Britain a duke has a title such as «the Duke of York». When you read a royal story, look for words like «Duke», «Prince» and «King». They tell you how important someone is.
explain: «Prince Harry married Meghan Markle at St George's Chapel, Windsor, on 19 May 2018, and they became the Duke and Duchess of Sussex.» The sentence does not say what a duke is, but the title tells you that the new Duke of Sussex is a very important person. Ask yourself: is this person ordinary, or high up?
explain: The word has more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one. «Kaliningrad ... as Königsberg it was once the capital of the dukes of Prussia.» Here dukes are rulers of a land. In old slang, «put up your dukes» means put up your fists and get ready to fight. Always check the words around the word before you decide.
fact: A duke is a man of the highest rank of the nobility, just below a prince.
fact: «Duke» is part of a title, such as «the Duke of York».
fact: In history, a duke ruled a small land called a duchy.
fact: «Dukes» can mean your fists in old slang, as in «put up your dukes».
fact: «Your Grace» is how you speak to a duke.
exercise: «Prince Harry became the Duke of Sussex.» What is a duke? | A type of royal castle | *A man of very high rank, just below a prince | A small farm animal | A teacher of history
exercise: Tom's brother shouts, «Put up your dukes!» What does dukes mean here? | *Your fists, so get ready to fight | Your dinner plates | Your ducks in the pond | Your gloves for a picnic
exercise: Which of these is a duke's title, like «the Duke of York»? | Captain Morgan | Doctor Jones | *Duke of Edinburgh | Chef Ramsay
test: In history, what did a duke rule? | A mountain village | A school | *A small land called a duchy | A river
test: The Doge in Venice was «a duke chosen for life». What does this tell you about the Doge? | *He was a duke, and he was chosen to rule for the rest of his life | He was a little boy | He was a fisherman | He was a king's cook
exam: What does «Duke» mean in «the Duke and Duchess of Sussex»? | A kind of bread | *A man of very high rank, a title used for a royal family member | A type of boat | A small castle
